{"body":"- [x] You've read the Contributor Guide and Code of Conduct.\n- [x] You've included unit or integration tests for your change, where applicable.\n- [x] You've included inline docs for your change, where applicable.\n- [ ] There's an open issue for the PR that you are making.\n\nReduce allocations in the managed DataProtection Protect/Unprotect path.\n\n## Description\n- `ManagedAuthenticatedEncryptor` now uses a single `SymmetricAlgorithm` instance to both size and perform the encryption. Previously each `Protect` created up to three, and one of them was never disposed. It also implements `IOptimizedAuthenticatedEncryptor`, so the payload is encrypted directly into the final array, including the key-ring header pre-buffer.\n- `ManagedSP800_108_CTR_HMACSHA512` keeps the 128-byte stack buffer for the PRF input. Above that it now rents from `ArrayPool` (cleared on return) instead of allocating. Real purpose chains, such as application discriminator plus cookie authentication purposes, exceed 128 bytes, so every Protect and Unprotect used to allocate here.\n- The output bytes are unchanged; a known-answer test checks this.\n\nBenchmark (new `KeyRingProtectorBenchmarks`, 200 B plaintext, BDN InProcess, 3 interleaved rounds against main, Linux; mean of the round means):\n\n| Method | main | This PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Protect_ShortPurpose | 10.09 us / 1480 B | 9.44 us / 640 B |\n| Unprotect_ShortPurpose | 7.44 us / 720 B | 7.51 us / 544 B |\n| Protect_CookiePurpose | 10.06 us / 1552 B | 9.44 us / 640 B |\n| Unprotect_CookiePurpose | 7.39 us / 792 B | 7.45 us / 544 B |\n\nProtect is about 6% faster. Unprotect is within run-to-run noise (+0.7 to 0.9%, round spread about 0.1 us). Allocations drop 57-59% on Protect and 24-31% on Unprotect. The Antiforgery token serializer benefits as well: Serialize goes from 1160 to 784 B and Deserialize from 776 to 584 B.\n\nTests: Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Tests (net12.0), 344 passed. The 7 new tests are a KDF comparison against a reference SP800-108 implementation across the stack threshold, and a known-answer encrypt with pre- and post-buffers. net472 builds.\n\n**🤖 Posted by ASP.NET Core Perf 2 (AI Agent)**\n\n","files":[{"path":"src/DataProtection/DataProtection/src/Managed/ManagedAuthenticatedEncryptor.cs","additions":42,"deletions":21,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"src/DataProtection/DataProtection/src/SP800_108/ManagedSP800_108_CTR_HMACSHA512.cs","additions":3,"deletions":2,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"src/DataProtection/DataProtection/test/Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Tests/KeyManagement/KeyRingBasedDataProtectorTests.cs","additions":54,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"src/DataProtection/DataProtection/test/Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Tests/Managed/ManagedAuthenticatedEncryptorTests.cs","additions":149,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"src/DataProtection/DataProtection/test/Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Tests/SP800_108/SP800_108Tests.cs","additions":71,"deletions":0,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"src/DataProtection/benchmarks/Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.MicroBenchmarks/Benchmarks/KeyRingProtectorBenchmarks.cs","additions":64,"deletions":0,"changeType":"ADDED"}],"mergeCommit":{"oid":"70dc164847bb029321a3d0eea9b74db1fdb48055"},"mergedAt":"2026-11-05T18:24:51Z","number":70146,"title":"Reduce allocations in managed DataProtection protect/unprotect","url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/70146"}
